= The Calvo Sotelo Assassination

In the early hours, a detachment of Assault Guards and allied militiamen - avenging the murder of one of their own lieutenants, José Castillo, by Falangist gunmen - take the monarchist leader José Calvo Sotelo from his home and shoot him. His body is dumped at a Madrid cemetery.

The killing of a sitting parliamentary deputy by men in government uniform electrifies the conspiracy that General Mola has spent months assembling. Officers who had hesitated now consider the moment decisive: if the state itself cannot guarantee the safety of a leader of the opposition, they argue, the state no longer deserves obedience. The rising that had been quietly gathering strength across the garrisons is now only a matter of days away.
